X1 Zihpm negative-control seed: event-mux 1<->2 swap
=====================================================

Swaps the arbiter-stall (event 1) and shared-bus-grant (event 2) decode in
csr_unit.vhd's hpm_fires(). With the swap, programming mhpmevent3=1 counts
GRANTS (one per shared transaction) instead of STALL CYCLES (several per
transaction), so counter3 no longer exceeds counter4 and extzihpm.S's
`bgeu s3, s2, zih_fail` assertion (stall_cycles > grant_count) trips -> FAIL.

Apply on top of the FIXED (committed) RTL, then rebuild the ON polarity and
run extzihpm; the probe must FAIL. Reverse to restore PASS.

REPRO
-----
  cd <worktree-root>
  # 1. flip ON polarity (isolated single-constant staging)
  sed -i 's/\(constant CORE_ENABLE_ZIHPM\t\t: boolean := \)false;/\1true;/' \
      hdl/common/MemoryMap.vhd
  # 2. apply the seed
  git apply verification/isa/negctrl/x1_zihpm_seed.patch
  # 3. run the ON probe (recompiles with the seeded RTL)
  cd xcelium/riscv_test/behavioral_mp
  printf '../rcf/xrv32ua-p-extzihpm.rcf\n' > /tmp/zihpm.txt
  TESTS_FILE=/tmp/zihpm.txt ./xrun_parallel.sh     # EXPECT: FAIL
  # 4. revert seed + polarity
  cd -
  git apply -R verification/isa/negctrl/x1_zihpm_seed.patch
  git checkout -- hdl/common/MemoryMap.vhd
  #    re-run step 3 -> EXPECT: PASS

--- a/hdl/common/vesta/csr_unit.vhd
+++ b/hdl/common/vesta/csr_unit.vhd
@@ -110,8 +110,8 @@ architecture behave of csr_unit is
                        trap_rose  : std_logic) return boolean is
     begin
         case sel is
-            when x"00000001" => return stall_lvl  = '1';  -- arbiter-stall cycles
-            when x"00000002" => return stall_fell = '1';  -- shared-bus grants (one per completed txn)
+            when x"00000001" => return stall_fell = '1';  -- NEGCTRL SEED: event 1<->2 swapped
+            when x"00000002" => return stall_lvl  = '1';  -- NEGCTRL SEED: event 1<->2 swapped
             when x"00000003" => return sleep_lvl  = '1';  -- sleep cycles
             when x"00000004" => return trap_rose  = '1';  -- trap entries taken
             when others      => return false;             -- 0 = off; unsupported = count nothing
